# Vercel hosts exactly ONE thing from this repository: the chat answer service
# (api/chat.js). The public site is static HTML on GitHub Pages and stays
# there - hard rule 1 - so nothing here serves pages.
#
# WRITTEN AS AN ALLOW-LIST, for the same reason .github/workflows/static.yml
# is: a new directory must be NAMED to ship. An exclude list publishes
# whatever nobody thought of, and P8-T3 exists because `path: '.'` once put
# editor/, server/, scripts/, docs/ and the vendored admin design on a
# customer-facing URL.
#
# TWO THINGS THIS DELIBERATELY KEEPS OUT:
#
#   api/cms.js - an unauthenticated serverless function from before this
#   rebuild. It sets Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * and accepts a POST from
#   anyone, storing the body in memory and handing it back on GET. It cannot
#   reach the real data, but it is an open write endpoint with no login and
#   there is no reason for it to exist on the internet. Vercel makes EVERY
#   file in api/ a live URL, so excluding the directory's contents and
#   re-including one file is the only safe shape here.
#
#   server/index.js, auth.js, db.js, sales.js, stock.js, reports.js - the
#   admin API. It is not a Vercel function and would not run, but it would be
#   fetchable as source. Phase 11 decides where that API lives; until then it
#   does not live here.

# Ignore everything at the root.
/*

# The chat function, and nothing else in api/.
!/api
/api/*
!/api/chat.js

# What it reads. server/chat.js is the service itself - no database, so it
# does not wait on Phase 11 - and data/ is the published content it answers
# from, already public on GitHub Pages, so this adds no exposure.
!/server
/server/*
!/server/chat.js

!/data

# Runtime config: the CORS headers and the includeFiles rule for data/**.
!/vercel.json

# Node runtime detection. server/chat.js itself requires only fs and path.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
